# Production build inputs. Loaded by Vite for `npm run build:production` only
# (loadEnv(mode, ...) in vite.config.js); preview, dev and test-production
# builds never read this file.
#
# Both values are public by definition - they are emitted into the shipped
# HTML as the canonical URL, the sitemap, the absolute social-card URLs, the
# closing repository link and the quickstart's `git clone` line. Nothing here
# is a secret, so this file is committed and a production build is
# reproducible from a clean checkout rather than from one machine's shell.
#
# EIF_SITE_URL must end in a slash and may carry a deployment sub-path; Vite's
# base is derived from it, which is what makes a project-page host such as
# GitHub Pages work without a custom domain. Change this one line to move the
# site to a different host.
#
# EIF_REPOSITORY_URL is deliberately not set here. The repository URL is a
# constant of the project rather than a per-deployment input, so it lives in
# vite.config.js and resolves in every mode, including dev; setting it in both
# places would only create somewhere for the two to drift apart. Export it as
# an environment variable to override it for one build.

EIF_SITE_URL=https://mike-arbuzov365.github.io/engineering-intelligence-framework/
